From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Net Mojo <56850867+netmojo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] wifi: brcmfmac: close dynamic netdevs before detach
 unregisters them

brcmf_detach() reads iflist[i] and ifp->ndev without RTNL or the wiphy
lock, then removes netdev interfaces unlocked. brcmf_p2p_del_vif(),
reached from NL80211_CMD_DEL_INTERFACE under both locks, can free a P2P
client or GO interface in that window. Only the P2P device interface,
which has no netdev, was removed under the locks.

Remove every interface except the primary one under RTNL and the wiphy
lock, and re-read the slot under them. Simply taking both locks around
brcmf_remove_interface(ifp, true) is not enough for a netdev that is up:
cfg80211_unregister_netdevice() closes it, and cfg80211's
NETDEV_GOING_DOWN and NETDEV_DOWN handlers take the wiphy mutex again.
The mutex is not recursive and RTNL is held, so every RTNL user on the
system hangs. awdl0 is a cfg80211 netdev and is up for the whole of an
AirDrop window, so a firmware crash during a window would reach this.

Do what nl80211_del_interface() does: dev_close() under RTNL alone,
then take the wiphy lock and unregister. brcmf_p2p_del_vif() needs RTNL
and the event worker has been cancelled, so the slot cannot change
between the two reads. The primary interface is still removed unlocked.
brcmf_del_if() takes RTNL itself to stop it.

Signed-off-by: Net Mojo <56850867+netmojo@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c        | 28 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index cea985e..44b26d0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -1641,20 +1641,32 @@ void brcmf_detach(struct device *dev)
 		if (!ifp)
 			continue;
 
-		if (ifp->ndev) {
+		if (i == 0) {
 			brcmf_remove_interface(ifp, false);
 			continue;
 		}
 
-		/* The P2P device interface has no netdev. Its removal can
-		 * race with NL80211_CMD_DEL_INTERFACE issued by a user space
-		 * process that is exiting (e.g. wpa_supplicant), which ends
-		 * in brcmf_p2p_del_vif() under RTNL and the wiphy mutex. If
-		 * both paths remove the interface, the wdev is unregistered
-		 * twice and the vif is used after being freed. Take the same
-		 * locks and re-read iflist, so only one path removes it.
+		/* Dynamic interfaces (P2P device, client and GO, AWDL) can be
+		 * removed concurrently by NL80211_CMD_DEL_INTERFACE from a user
+		 * space process that is exiting (e.g. wpa_supplicant), which
+		 * ends in brcmf_p2p_del_vif() under RTNL and the wiphy mutex.
+		 * If both paths remove the interface, the wdev is unregistered
+		 * twice and the vif is used after being freed. So iflist is
+		 * only read, and the interface only removed, under the same
+		 * locks.
+		 *
+		 * Close a netdev under RTNL alone first, as
+		 * nl80211_del_interface() does: closing an up wireless netdev
+		 * runs cfg80211's NETDEV_GOING_DOWN and NETDEV_DOWN handlers,
+		 * which take the wiphy mutex themselves. Unregistering it while
+		 * it is still up with that mutex held deadlocks, with RTNL held.
+		 * brcmf_p2p_del_vif() needs RTNL, and the event worker has been
+		 * cancelled, so the slot cannot change between the two reads.
 		 */
 		rtnl_lock();
+		ifp = drvr->iflist[i];
+		if (ifp && ifp->ndev)
+			dev_close(ifp->ndev);
 		wiphy_lock(drvr->wiphy);
 		ifp = drvr->iflist[i];
 		if (ifp)
